    Kevin : A story
    Kevin : “The fighters of Pomoland”
    You : Aw
    Kevin : I like this book
    Kevin : But it's people say its childish for my age
    Kevin : Everyone is already at a reading level of 7, I’m at 2, for my grade it's bad, but reading those older bigger kid books is so frustrating, why are there so many big words?
    You : I think just practicing reading should be fine
    Kevin : I guess..
    <<jump Kevin_Bully_Questions>>
-> You : So.. do you know James? <<if not $asked_kevin_james>>
    <<set $asked_kevin_james to true>>
    Kevin : James! He has a Ben 10 Watch!
    Kevin : Its so cool and it lights up too
    <<jump Kevin_Bully_Questions>>
-> You : So.. why don’t you play with your friends? <<if not $asked_kevin_friends>>
    <<set $asked_kevin_friends to true>>
    Kevin : Um..
    Kevin : Hm..
    Kevin : I mean I can’t really 
    <<jump Kevin_Bully_Questions>>
-> You : Okay, I know you can read but lets do a writing challenge!
    Kevin : A writing challenge?
    Kevin : You’re on!
    Kevin : I’m gonna win
    <<start_minigame MinigameManager "words">>
===

title: Kevin_Bully_Midpoint
---
Kevin : Uhhhhhhhmm..
Kevin : A... C... T...
Kevin : Taac?
You : Close, its spelled C A t
Kevin : This game is broken!
Kevin : The letters are wrong!
You : They're just mixed up.
You : Try the first letter first.
Kevin : ...I can't read when they're mixed up.
Kevin : *Sigh*
You : Why do you care what Daisy thinks?
Kevin : Uhhhhhhhh.
Kevin : And she has a big book.
You : You like her?
Kevin : NO!?
You : What if you were just nicer to her?
Kevin : Nicer?
Kevin : James says if you're nice, nobody remembers you.
You : But Daisy thinks you hate her..
Kevin : I do like her!
You : Then say that..
